        "title": "fix(agent-core): avoid a crash when empty output has a negative line limit",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where developers using the agent-core truncation helper would see a crash when empty output is evaluated with a negative line limit.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe head-truncation path now handles empty input before calculating first-line bytes and returns the existing structured truncation result. Valid non-empty truncation behavior is unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAgent-core consumers now receive truncation metadata instead of an exception for this empty-output boundary case.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Head: `8ed74057b1253f2740186d334bd7ac82299b947f`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/agent-core/src/harness/utils/truncate.test.ts` (9 passed)\n- `git diff --check`\n- `python .agents\\\\skills\\\\autoreview\\\\scripts\\\\autoreview --mode branch --base upstream/main` (clean; no accepted/actionable findings)\n",
